Level 3. wdmatch
Assignment name: wdmatch
Expected file: wdmatch.c
Allowed functions: write

Write a program that takes two strings and checks whether it is possible to write the first string using characters from the second string, while respecting the order in which these characters appear in the second string.
If it is possible, the program displays the first string, followed by a newline.
Otherwise, it displays only a newline.
If the number of arguments is not 2, it displays only a newline.

int     main(int argc, char **argv)
{       
        int     i;
        int     j;
        
        i = 0;
        j = 0;
        if (argc != 3)
        {
                write(1, "\n", 1);
                return (0);
        }
        while (argv[2][j] != '\0')
        {       
                if (argv[1][i] == argv[2][j])
                        i++;
                j++;
        }       
        if (argv[1][i] == '\0')
        {       
                j = 0;
                while (argv[1][j] != '\0')
                {
                        write(1, &argv[1][j], 1);
                        j++;
                }
        }
        write(1, "\n", 1);
        return (0);
}
